// spec: an `else` indented as an outer `if`'s that belongs to the inner `if` it follows (C++'s dangling else) is an error (kovarex, 2026-11-11, item 4 of thread D's survey of missing checks; clang's -Wdangling-else warns of every such else): braces on the inner `if` say which
// error: else_indented_as_an_outer_if_is_error.kpp:9: error: this `else` is indented as the `if` on line 6, but belongs to the `if` on line 7: put that inner `if` in braces, or indent the `else` as its own
int pick(bool a, bool b)
{
  int r = 0;
  if (a)
    if (b)
      r = 1;
  else
    r = 2;
  return r;
}
int main() { return pick(true, false); }
